---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About — Waking Matter"
  description="Waking Matter explores systems for cumulative intelligence. Contact hello@wakingmatter.com."
  canonical="https://wakingmatter.com/about/"
  current="about"
>
  <main id="content" class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="label">About</p>
      <h1>A small effort, held to a long problem.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Waking Matter is a research effort exploring systems for cumulative
        intelligence. We are early. This page is an account of that, not a
        portrait of an institution we have not built.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-page split">
      <p class="label">What we are</p>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          We explore systems that can preserve, inherit, and compound useful
          learning across agents, models, and time. The short form is the line
          we use everywhere else: building systems for cumulative intelligence.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is a direction of work, not a catalogue of products, a roster,
          or a list of results. We will publish notes when we have something
          careful to say. We will not fill the silence with a team page, a
          customer list, or a simulated lab.
        </p>
        <p>
          The public surface is this site —
          <a href="/research/">research questions</a>,
          <a href="/notes/">notes</a>, an address —
          <a href="mailto:hello@wakingmatter.com">hello@wakingmatter.com</a> —
          and whatever we actually write. If you are looking for a demo, a
          hiring page, or a claim of novelty, you will not find it here.
        </p>
        <p>
          The traits we hold ourselves to are precision, depth, and composure.
          They are standards for how we think and write, not decorations for a
          brand that wants to look serious.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
